mary card’s balance, and any late‑payment penalties or interest charges are applied exclusively to the main cardholder.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_5f31fc26\", \"content\": \"Question: What factors determine the monthly fee for transferring my balance to a Horizon Bank credit card?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, the monthly charge for balance transfers is calculated based on the outstanding balance. Prior to the final month of your tenure, a monthly fee of either {{faq_5f31fc26_001}} for transfers approved before August {{faq_5f31fc26_002}}, {{faq_5f31fc26_003}}, or {{faq_5f31fc26_004}} for transfers approved on or after August {{faq_5f31fc26_005}}, {{faq_5f31fc26_006}}, will be applied to your Horizon Bank credit card statement. This fee will be included in the minimum payment due. In the last month of your tenure, or if you opt to repay your balance early, the remaining outstanding balance will be charged to your statement, along with a {{faq_5f31fc26_007}} fee on the outstanding amount, which will also be included in the minimum payment due. For detailed information, please consult the Balance Transfer Product Terms and Key Facts document provided by Horizon Bank.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_25ce7c68\", \"content\": \"Question: What is the process for requesting a waiver of charges on my Horizon Bank credit card account?\\n\\nAnswer: To request a waiver of a late payment fee, simply send a message through the Horizon App's in-app chat service, specifying 'fee waiver' in your query. Our team will carefully review your request and provide an update via push notification within {{faq_25ce7c68_001}} working days.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_3bade286\", \"content\": \"Question: Do the zero-fee benefits associated with my Horizon card have an expiration date?\\n\\nAnswer: As a valued Horizon Bank customer, you can rest assured that the zero-fee privileges, including no annual fee, foreign transaction fee, card replacement fee, or overlimit fee, are a permanent feature of your