obile app to view current annual fee charges\", \"policy\": \"Annual fees are charged once per year on the anniversary of your credit card account opening date\", \"conceptual\": \"An annual fee is a yearly cost for maintaining your credit card account and accessing its benefits\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_5f31fc26\", \"content\": \"Question: What factors determine the monthly fee for transferring my balance to a Horizon Bank credit card?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, the monthly charge for balance transfers is calculated based on the outstanding balance. Prior to the final month of your tenure, a monthly fee of either {{faq_5f31fc26_001}} for transfers approved before August {{faq_5f31fc26_002}}, {{faq_5f31fc26_003}}, or {{faq_5f31fc26_004}} for transfers approved on or after August {{faq_5f31fc26_005}}, {{faq_5f31fc26_006}}, will be applied to your Horizon Bank credit card statement. This fee will be included in the minimum payment due. In the last month of your tenure, or if you opt to repay your balance early, the remaining outstanding balance will be charged to your statement, along with a {{faq_5f31fc26_007}} fee on the outstanding amount, which will also be included in the minimum payment due. For detailed information, please consult the Balance Transfer Product Terms and Key Facts document provided by Horizon Bank.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_e5db6d91\", \"content\": \"Question: Are there any fees associated with obtaining a supplementary Horizon card?\\n\\nAnswer: - Horizon Bank does not levy any issuance or annual fees for an additional card. All expenses incurred on the supplementary card are combined with the primary card’s balance, and any late‑payment penalties or interest charges are applied exclusively to the main cardholder.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_3d77cf86\", \"content\": \"Question: When I have both a Horizon credit card and a Horizon debit card, how is the minimum monthly spend determined?\\n\\nAnswer: - In the month you are issued your second card, the minimum spend threshold follows the rules of the first card you already hold, recognizing that the new card may not be used right away.\\n- Beginning with the next calendar month, the spend requirement will be set according to the minimum spend policy of the Horizon credit card.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_df0e6cbd\", \"content\": \"Question: What are the charges associated with withdrawing cash using my Horizon card?\\n\\nAnswer: As of {{faq_df0e6cbd_001}} February {{faq_df0e6cbd_002}}, Horizon Bank imposes a cash advance fee of {{faq_df0e6cbd_003}} on the withdrawn amount, although transactions below {{faq_df0e6cbd_004}} are exempt from this charge. Additionally, a daily interest rate of {{faq_df0e6cbd_005}} (equivalent to {{faq_df0e6cbd_006}} per annum) is applied to the withdrawn amount, starting from the transaction posting date until the payment is made in full. Please note that from {{faq_df0e6cbd_007}} July {{faq_df0e6cbd_008}}, your Effective Interest Rate will be tailored to your individual credit profile, ranging from {{faq_df0e6cbd_009}} to {{faq_df0e6cbd_010}} per annum.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents.\n        - Each Task Input may include `prior_sufficiency_audit_history` from\n          earlier attempts for the same task in this turn. Read it before\n          judging the current candidates and remain consistent with its prior\n          sufficiency judgments. This history is internal audit context only;\n          it is not customer-facing evidence and does not authorize any new\n          factual claim.\n        - Classify each task as SUFFICIENT, PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, or\n          INSUFFICIENT. Judge whether the sup