t card'.\\n   * Choose your savings account from the available options to complete the payment.\\n   * Review the transfer details carefully before confirming the transaction.\\n\\n   Alternatively, you can pay using other bank accounts. This can be done in two main ways: by adding your Horizon credit card as a local transfer recipient or as a credit card payment recipient. The steps may vary depending on your bank's app, but generally, you will need to add your Horizon credit card details as a new payee or recipient and then initiate the transfer.\\n\\n   For payments made through other banks' apps, the processing time may take up to {{faq_a5ab2ed8_001}} working days. It's essential to note that your credit card payment is due on the date you selected when you first applied for your Horizon credit card. Failure to make payment by the due date may result in late payment fees and interest on the outstanding amount. Even if you make the minimum payment on time, you will still be charged interest on the remaining balance.\\n\\n   For detailed instructions on paying through specific banks like DBS/POSB, UOB, OCBC, and Standard Chartered Bank, as well as information on card pairing for Trust Link credit card holders, please refer to our FAQs on the Horizon Bank website or through the Horizon App. Remember, timely payments help you avoid additional fees and interest charges.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents.\n        - Each Task Input may include `prior_sufficiency_audit_history` from\n          earlier attempts for the same task in this turn. Read it before\n          judging the current candidates and remain consistent with its prior\n          sufficiency judgments. This history is internal audit context only;\n          it is not custo