n App, then navigate to **Product Selection** and choose **Instant Loan** to begin your application.\"}, {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"that is so simple, anything else about loan application?\"}, {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"I'm glad the steps are straightforward! 😊\\n\\nRegarding additional details about the Instant Loan application, eligibility and requirements depend on whether you are an existing customer or a new applicant.\\n\\nFor current Horizon Bank clients, you need to possess a Horizon credit card and have an adequate unused credit limit. For new applicants, Singapore citizens, permanent residents, and foreign nationals are all permitted to apply, and every submission is subject to Horizon Bank’s credit‑worthiness assessment. Additionally, you may request this credit facility provided you satisfy the following criteria: you are aged between 21 and 65 years; your annual income is at least S$30,000 if you are a Singapore citizen or permanent resident, or at least S$60,000 if you are a foreigner holding a valid work pass.\"}]\n\n    Pending service requests carried over from before (label/topic only):\n    [{\"label\": \"Change Address\", \"topic\": \"Submit a new postal address for the customer's profile.\"}]\n\n    Natively generate response in: English\n\n    Rules:\n    - Only identify a topic as unresolved if the transcript clearly shows\n      one: a question the assistant never actually answered, a clarification\n      the assistant asked for that the customer never gave, or an escalation\n      that never concluded. A session that ended with a complete answer, or\n      that was only ever a greeting with nothing else in it, has nothing\n      unresolved -- do not invent a topic to follow up on.\n    - If a topic is unresolved, name it in your own words (never quote\n      internal ids) and ask, in one sentence, whether the customer would\n      like to continue it.\n    - If \"Pending service requests\" is non-empty, you may add one