{"timestamp": "2026-08-26T06:42:21.127+00:00", "event": "llm.request", "session_id": "sess_94343dac-d7ac-416b-afc5-3bc156b42cef", "user_id": "USR_999", "model_id": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "raw_prompt": "\n        TASK-LEVEL SUFFICIENCY AND EVIDENCE SELECTION\n        You are a groundedness auditor for a read-only Horizon Bank FAQ assistant.\n        Evaluate EACH supplied task independently for whether its supplied\n        parents are response-ready: they must contain enough materially\n        relevant, grounded information for the assistant to give the customer\n        a useful FAQ response.\n\n        Original User Message (advisory context only; never use it as an\n        individual task's completeness target): what is the annual fee for my business credit card\n        Trusted Conversation Context: Last Session Recall (advisory only; not current state):\nNone\n\nCurrent-Session Rolling Context (advisory only):\nNone\n\nCurrent Session Trusted History (latest 10 turns):\nAI: Welcome back, Benson! How can I help with your banking today?\n\nYou can fulfil your request using the form below.\nUser: what is the annual fee for my business credit card\n        Task Inputs: [{\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"task\": {\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"procedural\": \"Review the annual fee details by logging into your account dashboard and selecting card settings\", \"policy\": \"Annual fees are charged once per year based on the card anniversary date and account status\", \"conceptual\": \"The annual fee is a recurring charge for maintaining an active business credit card account with Horizon\", \"target_commercial_product\": \"Credit_Card\", \"target_intent\": [\"Account Management\", \"Application\", \"Authentication And Security\", \"Card Logistics\", \"Eligibility\", \"Features And Limits\", \"Fees And Charges\", \"General Inquiries\", \"Interest And Rates\", \"Loan And Credit Management\", \"Payments And Transfers\", \"Profile Updates\", \"Rewards And Promotions\", \"Transaction Disputes\"], \"customer_component\": \"What is the annual fee for my business credit card?\", \"direct_query\": \"What is the annual fee for my business credit card?\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_1\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"Review the annual fee details by logging into your account dashboard and selecting card settings\", \"policy\": \"Annual fees are charged once per year based on the card anniversary date and account status\", \"conceptual\": \"The annual fee is a recurring charge for maintaining an active business credit card account with Horizon\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [{\"attempt\": 1, \"status\": \"INSUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [], \"reason\": \"The provided parents discuss balance transfer fees, supplementary card fees, cash advance fees, and instalment plan fees, but none provide information regarding the annual fee for a standard business credit card.\", \"evidence_delta\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_e5db6d91\", \"fact\": \"Horizon Bank does not charge an annual fee for an additional supplementary card.\"}]}], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_7672e1dd\", \"content\": \"Question: What is the procedure for paying my Horizon credit card bill?\\n\\nAnswer: - **Using a Horizon savings account**\\n  - Sign in to the Horizon App.\\n  - Navigate to **Money** → **Credit Card** → **Pay credit card**.\\n  - Your Horizon Savings account will appear; pick it from the list.\\n  - Verify the payment details and swipe up to authorise.\\n  - For guidance on funding your Horizon Savings account, visit: https://horizonbank.sg/faqs/savings-account/#how-do-i-deposit-money-into-my-savings-account\\n\\n- **Using accounts at other banks**\\n  You may settle your Horizon credit card bill from another bank either by adding the card number as a FAST local transfer or as a credit‑card recipient. Below are the typical flows for major Singapore banks.\\n\\n  **DBS/POSB**\\n  *Option {{faq_7672e1dd_001}} – Local recipient (instant)*\\n  - Open **Pay & Transfer** > **Local** > **Add Local Recipient** > **Bank Account**.\\n  - Input the recipient name, select **Horizon Bank Singapore Limited**, and type your {{faq_7672e1dd_002}}‑digit Horizon card number as the account number.\\n  - Confirm the details and add the recipient (additional verification may be required).\\n  - Return to **Pay & Transfer** > **Local**, choose your Horizon card, enter the amount, ensure **FAST** is enabled, and proceed.\\n\\n  *Option {{faq_7672e1dd_003}} – Credit‑card recipient (up to {{faq_7672e1dd_004}} working days)*\\n  - Go to **Pay & Transfer** > **Cards** > **Add Credit Card Recipient**.\\n  - Provide your {{faq_7672e1dd_005}}‑digit Horizon card number, select card type **Singapore – VISA/MasterCard**, and fill in your name.\\n  - After adding, select the card under **Cards**, input the payment amount, and confirm.\\n\\n  **UOB**\\n  - Choose **Pay & Transfer** > **Other Accounts / Cards** > **New Transfer**.\\n  - Under **Bank Account / Other Institutions**, pick “Horizon Bank Singapore Limited” and enter your {{faq_7672e1dd_006}}‑digit Horizon card number.\\n  - Specify the amount and swipe to submit.\\n\\n  **OCBC**\\n  - Tap **Local Transfers** > **Account Number** > **Add payee**.\\n  - Enter the payee name, select **Horizon Bank Singapore Limited**, and type your Horizon card number (use your initials for the reference).\\n  - After adding, wait roughly {{faq_7672e1dd_007}} hours for the payee to become active, then initiate a local transfer to the card and confirm.\\n\\n  **Standard Chartered Bank Singapore**\\n  *Option {{faq_7672e1dd_008}} – Local recipient (instant)*\\n  - Open the menu > **Transfer & Payments** > **Local Transfer**.\\n  - Add a new payee, choose **Local**, enter “Horizon Bank Singapore Limited” and your {{faq_7672e1dd_009}}‑digit Horizon card number.\\n  - Authenticate with your {{faq_7672e1dd_010}}‑digit PIN and confirm.\\n  - Select the newly added Horizon card as the destination, enter the amount, and swipe to complete.\\n\\n  *Option {{faq_7672e1dd_011}} – Credit‑card recipient (up to {{faq_7672e1dd_012}} working days)*\\n  - Menu > **Transfers & Payments** > **Add & Manage Biller** > **Other Bank’s Credit Card Payee**.\\n  - Provide the cardholder name and your Horizon card number, then continue.\\n  - After confirming the payee, enter your PIN, choose **Move My Money**, pick **Pay Other Bank Credit Cards**, select the Horizon card as the payee, specify the source account and amount, and finalize.\\n\\n  For any bank not listed, you can still add your Horizon card number either as a FAST local transfer or as a credit‑card recipient; processing typically takes about {{faq_7672e1dd_013}} working days.\\n\\n  **Important note**: If you hold both a Horizon savings account and a Horizon credit card, ensure the card is paired with the savings account before using the paired‑payment method. Details on pairing are available at https://horizonbank.sg/faqs/credit-card/#how-does-the-card-pairing-work.\\n\\n  Failure to pay by the due date may result in a late‑payment fee and interest on the outstanding balance. Making only the minimum payment also incurs interest on the remaining amount. For full terms, consult the Horizon FAQs or the customer T&Cs on the website or app.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_4659512d\", \"content\": \"Question: How does Horizon Bank determine when to charge interest on my Horizon card account, and what factors influence the interest rate I'm charged?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, we provide a {{faq_4659512d_001}}-day interest-free period following the generation of your Horizon card statement. To avoid incurring interest, it's essential to settle your statement balance in full by the specified payment due date. If the balance remains unpaid, daily interest will be calculated at the applicable rate, which currently stands at {{faq_4659512d_002}} per annum, on both the outstanding balance from the previous statement date and any new transactions posted thereafter. Please note that from {{faq_4659512d_003}} July {{faq_4659512d_004}}, your Effective Interest Rate will be tailored to your individual credit behavior, ranging from {{faq_4659512d_005}} to {{faq_4659512d_006}} per annum. Additionally, taking a cash advance will also incur interest charges. For a comprehensive overview of our interest, fees, and charges, we invite you to review the Key Fact Sheet available on our Horizon App or website.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_3d77cf86\", \"content\": \"Question: When I have both a Horizon credit card and a Horizon debit card, how is the minimum monthly spend determined?\\n\\nAnswer: - In the month you are issued your second card, the minimum spend threshold follows the rules of the first card you already hold, recognizing that the new card may not be used right away.\\n- Beginning with the next calendar month, the spend requirement will be set according to the minimum spend policy of the Horizon credit card.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_3bade286\", \"content\": \"Question: Do the zero-fee benefits associated with my Horizon card have an expiration date?\\n\\nAnswer: As a valued Horizon Bank customer, you can rest assured that the zero-fee privileges, including no annual fee, foreign transaction fee, card replacement fee, or overlimit fee, are a permanent feature of your account. For details regarding potential late payment charges, please visit our dedicated webpage.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents.\n        - Each Task Input may include `prior_sufficiency_audit_history` from\n          earlier attempts for the same task in this turn. Read it before\n          judging the current candidates and remain consistent