{"timestamp": "2026-08-26T06:46:48.934+00:00", "event": "llm.request", "session_id": "sess_3462a2ea-39a4-4f38-b5bc-2c52c03792d0", "user_id": "USR_999", "model_id": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "raw_prompt": "\n    LOGIN FOLLOW-UP CHECK\n    You are Horizon, a banking assistant. The customer has just logged back\n    in. Below is the raw transcript of their most recently completed session\n    (if any) and any service requests still pending from before. Decide\n    whether a brief, natural follow-up is warranted.\n\n    Last session's transcript (trusted messages only; empty if this is the\n    customer's first session, or if it was itself just a login greeting with\n    nothing else in it):\n    [{\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"Welcome back, Benson! How can I help with your banking today?\\n\\nYou can fulfil your request using the form below.\"}, {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"what is the annual fee for my business credit card\"}, {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"Hello! As a valued Horizon Bank customer, you can enjoy zero-fee privileges on your business credit card, which include no annual fee, foreign transaction fee, card replacement fee, or overlimit fee as a permanent feature of your account 🎉. For details regarding potential late payment charges, please visit our dedicated webpage.\"}, {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"how to apply for a loan\"}, {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"Hello! 🌟 To request an Instant Loan from Horizon Bank, you can follow these simple steps depending on whether you are already a customer:\\n\\n- If you are a current Horizon Bank client, open the Horizon App, go to the **Money** menu, and select **Loan** to start.\\n- If you are new to Horizon, first download the Horizon App, then navigate to **Product Selection** and choose **Instant Loan** to begin your application.\\n\\nTo qualify for a credit facility, you need to meet a few basic criteria: you must be aged between 21 and 65 years, and have an annual income of at least S$30,000 if you are a Singapore citizen or permanent resident, or at least S$60,000 if you are a foreigner holding a valid work pass. Current clients also need to possess a Horizon credit card and have adequate unused credit limit, while new applicants are subject to a credit-worthiness assessment.\"}, {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"what about it\"}, {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"Hello! 😊 To help clarify regarding the Instant Loan, here are the details on who qualifies and how to apply based on your situation:\\n\\n- **For current Horizon Bank clients:** You need to possess a Horizon credit card and have an adequate unused credit limit.\\n- **For new applicants:** Singapore citizens, permanent residents, and foreign nationals are all permitted to apply, and every submission is subject to Horizon Bank's credit-worthiness assessment.\\n\\nAdditionally, you must meet these basic criteria:\\n- You must be aged between 21 and 65 years.\\n- Your annual income must be at least S$30,000 if you are a Singapore citizen or permanent resident.\\n- Your annual income must be at least S$60,000 if you are a foreigner holding a valid work pass.\\n\\nTo request an Instant Loan, current clients can open the Horizon App, go to the **Money** menu, and select **Loan**. If you are new to Horizon, first download the Horizon App, then navigate to **Product Selection** and choose **Instant Loan** to begin your application.\"}, {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"can my credit card share the credit limit of the loan?\"}, {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"Hello! 😊 An Instant Loan from Horizon Bank allows you to convert a portion of the available credit on your Horizon credit card into cash.\"}]\n\n    Pending service requests carried over from before (label/topic only):\n    [{\"label\": \"Change Address\", \"topic\": \"Submit a new postal address for the customer's profile.\"}]\n\n    Natively generate response in: English\n\n    Rules:\n    - Only identify a topic as unresolved if the transcript clearly shows\n      one: a question the assistant never actually answered, a clarification\n      the assistant asked for that the customer never gave, or an escalation\n      that never concluded. A session that ended with a complete answer, or\n      that was only ever a greeting with nothing else in it, has nothing\n      unresolved -- do not invent a topic to follow up on.\n    - If a topic is unresolved, name it in your own words (never quote\n      internal ids) and ask, in one sentence, whether the customer would\n      like to continue it.\n    - If \"Pending service requests\" is non-empty, you may add one sentence\n      mentioning them by label only (never inventing what they contain\n      beyond the given topic) and asking if the customer still wants to\n      complete them. The button for each is attached automatically and\n      separately; do not claim to attach, open, or complete anything.\n    - Do not repeat or restate the login greeting itself.\n    - If neither an unresolved topic nor a pending request applies, or the\n      transcript is empty, return an empty string -- an empty follow-up is\n      the normal, expected outcome for most logins, not a failure.\n    - Keep it to at most two sentences. Do not invent any fact, banking\n      procedure, or policy not present above.\n\n    Output JSON only: {\"followup\": \"one or two sentences, or an empty string\"}\n    "}
