ransfers\", \"Profile Updates\", \"Rewards And Promotions\", \"Transaction Disputes\"], \"customer_component\": \"What is the annual fee for my business credit card?\", \"direct_query\": \"What is the annual fee for my business credit card?\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_1\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"Review the annual fee details by logging into your account dashboard or checking your monthly statement\", \"policy\": \"Annual fees for business credit cards are charged once per year on the account anniversary date\", \"conceptual\": \"An annual fee is a yearly charge applied to credit card accounts for maintaining the card membership\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [{\"attempt\": 1, \"status\": \"INSUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [], \"reason\": \"None of the provided parents contain information regarding the annual fee for a business credit card. The parents discuss balance transfer fees, supplementary card fees, cash advance fees, and instalment plan fees, none of which address the general annual fee for a business credit card.\", \"evidence_delta\": []}], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_7672e1dd\", \"content\": \"Question: What is the procedure for paying my Horizon credit card bill?\\n\\nAnswer: - **Using a Horizon savings account**\\n  - Sign in to the Horizon App.\\n  - Navigate to **Money** → **Credit Card** → **Pay credit card**.\\n  - Your Horizon Savings account will appear; pick it from the list.\\n  - Verify the payment details and swipe up to authorise.\\n  - For guidance on funding your Horizon Savings account, visit: https://horizonbank.sg/faqs/savings-account/#how-do-i-deposit-money-into-my-savings-account\\n\\n- **Using accounts at other banks**\\n  You may settle your Horizon credit card bill from another bank either by adding the card number as a FAST local transfer or as a credit‑card recipient. Below are the typical flows for major Singapore banks.\\n\\n  **DBS/POSB**\\n  *Option {{faq_7672e1dd_001}} – Local recipient (instant)*\\n  - Open **Pay & Transfer** > **Local** > **Add Local Recipient** > **Bank Account**.\\n  - Input the recipient name, select **Horizon Bank Singapore Limited**, and type your {{faq_7672e1dd_002}}‑digit Horizon card number as the account number.\\n  - Confirm the details and add the recipient (additional verification may be required).\\n  - Return to **Pay & Transfer** > **Local**, choose your Horizon card, enter the amount, ensure **FAST** is enabled, and proceed.\\n\\n  *Option {{faq_7672e1dd_003}} – Credit‑card recipient (up to {{faq_7672e1dd_004}} working days)*\\n  - Go to **Pay & Transfer** > **Cards** > **Add Credit Card Recipient**.\\n  - Provide your {{faq_7672e1dd_005}}‑digit Horizon card number, select card type **Singapore – VISA/MasterCard**, and fill in your name.\\n  - After adding, select the card under **Cards**, input the payment amount, and confirm.\\n\\n  **UOB**\\n  - Choose **Pay & Transfer** > **Other Accounts / Cards** > **New Transfer**.\\n  - Under **Bank Account / Other Institutions**, pick “Horizon Bank Singapore Limited” and enter your {{faq_7672e1dd_006}}‑digit Horizon card number.\\n  - Specify the amount and swipe to submit.\\n\\n  **OCBC**\\n  - Tap **Local Transfers** > **Account Number** > **Add payee**.\\n  - Enter the payee name, select **Horizon Bank Singapore Limited**, and type your Horizon card number (use your initials for the reference).\\n  - After adding, wait roughly {{faq_7672e1dd_007}} hours for the payee to become active, then initiate a local transfer to the card and confirm.\\n\\n  **Standard Chartered Bank Singapore**\\n  *Option {{faq_7672e1dd_008}} – Local recipient (instant)*\\n  - Open the menu > **Transfer & Payments** > **Local Transfer**.\\n  - Add a new payee, choose **Local**, enter “Horizon Bank Singapore Limited” and your {{faq_7672e1dd_009}}‑digit Horizon card number.\\n  - Authenticate with your {{faq_7672e1dd_010}}‑digit PIN and confirm.\\n  - Select the newly added Horizon card as the destination, enter the amount, and swipe to complete.\\n\\n  *Option {{faq_7672e1dd_011}} – Credit‑card recipient (up to {{faq_7672e1dd_012}} working days)*\\n  - Menu > **Transfers & Payments** > **Add & Manage Biller** > **Other Bank’s Credit Card Payee**.\\n  - Provide the cardholder name and your Horizon card number, then continue.\\n  - After confirming the payee, enter your PIN, choose **Move My Money**, pick **Pay Other Bank Credit Cards**, select the Horizon card as the payee, specify the source account and amount, and finalize.\\n\\n  For any bank not listed, you can still add your Horizon card number either as a FAST local transfer or as a credit‑card recipient; processing typically takes about {{faq_7672e1dd_013}} working days.\\n\\n  **Important note**: If you hold both a Horizon savings account and a Horizon credit card, ensure the card is paired with the savings account before using the paired‑payment method. Details on pairing are available at https://horizonbank.sg/faqs/credit-card/#how-does-the-card-pairing-work.\\n\\n  Failure to pay by the due date may result in a late‑payment fee and interest on the outstanding balance. Making only the minimum payment also incurs interest on the remaining amount. For full terms, consult the Horizon FAQs or the customer T&Cs on the website or app.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_4659512d\", \"content\": \"Question: How does Horizon Bank determine when to charge interest on my Horizon card account, and what factors influence the interest rate I'm charged?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, we provide a {{faq_4659512d_001}}-day interest-free period following the generation of your Horizon card statement. To avoid incurring interest, it's essential to settle your statement balance in full by the specified payment due date. If the balance remains unpaid, daily interest will be calculated at the applicable rate, which currently stands at {{faq_4659512d_002}} per annum, on both the outstanding balance from the previous statement date and any new transactions posted thereafter. Please note that from {{faq_4659512d_003}} July {{faq_4659512d_004}}, your Effective Interest Rate will be tailored to your individual credit behavior, ranging from {{faq_4659512d_005}} to {{faq_4659512d_006}} per annum. Additionally, taking a cash advance will also incur interest charges. For a comprehensive overview of our interest, fees, and charges, we invite you to review the Key Fact Sheet available on our Horizon App or website.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_3d77cf86\", \"content\": \"Question: When I have both a Horizon credit card and a Horizon debit card, how is the minimum monthly spend determined?\\n\\nAnswer: - In the month you are issued your second card, the minimum spend threshold follows the rules of the first card you already hold, recognizing that the new card may not be used right away.\\n- Beginning with the next calendar month, the spend requirement will be set according to the minimum spend policy of the Horizon credit card.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_3bade286\", \"content\": \"Question: Do the zero-fee benefits associated with my Horizon card have an expiration date?\\n\\nAnswer: As a valued Horizon Bank customer, you can rest assured that the zero-fee privileges, including no annual fee, foreign transaction fee, card replacement fee, or overlimit fee, are a permanent feature of your account. For details regarding potential late payment charges, please visit our dedicated webpage.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents.\n        - Each Task Input may include `prior_sufficiency_audit_history` from\n          earlier attempts for the same task in this turn. Read it before\n          judging the current candidates and remain consistent with its prior\n          sufficiency judgments. This history is internal audit context only;\n          it is not customer-facing evidence and does not authorize any new\n          factual claim.\n        - Classify each task as SUFFICIENT, PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, or\n          INSUFFICIENT. Judge whether the supplied parents provide useful,\n          materially relevant information for the task—not whether they repeat\n          the customer's wording or explicitly resolve every possible\n          interpretation of the customer's question.\n        - PARTIAL-EVIDENCE DECISION ORDER: First identify whether any supplied\n          parent contains a factual proposition directly relevant to a\n          meaningful aspect of the customer's resolved request. If one does,\n          do not return INSUFFICIENT merely because the parent cannot determine\n          the customer's requested outcome, permission, eligibility,\n          exception, legality, preferred action, or other broader conclusion.\n          Retain that parent as PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT when its supported fact\n          can be truthfully presented as useful, bounded Horizon guidance\n          while another material aspect remains unresolved. Continue retrieval\n          for the unresolved aspect.\n        - Return INSUFFICIENT only when no supplied parent contains any\n          factual proposition that can be truthfully and materially presented\n          in relation to the resolved request. A parent is not material merely\n          because it concerns the same product: its supported fact must\n          directly concern the same topic, condition, process, boundary, or\n          factual premise in the customer's request.\n        - SUFFICIENT: the selected parents contain enough grounded information\n          for a useful response to the `customer_component`, even when that\n          response is an explicit policy boundary, limit, condition,\n          restriction, or other related factual information rather than a\n          literal yes/no answer. The response generator will state only what\n          the evidence supports and must not invent a broader conclusion.\n        \nPRECISION REFERENCE CONTRACT:\n- A token matching `{{faq_*}}` is a database-backed exact-value reference,\n  never missing, unknown, incomplete, or a customer-visible template.\n- It may represent an exact amount, rate, limit, date, threshold, or other\n  precise value. Treat it as the underlying approved fact for relevance,\n  sufficiency, generation, compliance, and groundedness.\n- Preserve the token exactly in any draft. The backend deterministically\n  substitutes its authoritative value only after outbound validation.\n- Never reject, weaken, or describe evidence as unavailable merely because the\n  exact value is represented by a `{{faq_*}}` token.\n- Within the stated scope, \"up to {{faq_*}}\" expresses an exact maximum. It\n  supports the bounded conclusion that the stated coverage or benefit does not\n  exceed that value. It does not, by itself, support claims about applications,\n  approvals, denials, exceptions, or who controls the limit.\n\n        - PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT: selected parents provide grounded, material\n          information for one meaningful part of the `customer_component`,\n          while another material part has no useful related evidence. Select\n          only the supporting parent IDs; the backend will retain them while\n          retrieval continues.\n        - INSUFFICIENT: the supplied parents provide no grounded, materially\n          relevant information that could be usefully presented in response to\n          the `customer_component`.\n        - Use the ordinary meaning of explicit policy boundaries, quantities,\n          conditions, and restrictions when deciding whether a task is\n          response-ready. Do not require a parent to restate the customer's\n          question or explicitly state the customer's requested conclusion.\n          For example, an explicit statutory maximum or fixed policy limit is\n          response-ready for a question about raising that limit, even if the\n          parent does not separately say \"no\" or describe every possible\n          external arrangement.\n          Preserve each parent's scope and do not infer facts beyond it.\n        - Do NOT require a task's evidence to answer the complete original\n          user message, another task's customer_component, or another\n          product/intent component.\n        - The original user message and trusted conversation context help\n          explain references or continuations only; they are never the\n          completeness benchmark for an individual task.\n        - Return one result for every supplied task_id.\n        - For SUFFICIENT or PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, return only parent IDs from\n          that exact task that materially support the answer. At least one ID\n          is required for either status.\n        - For PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT or INSUFFICIENT, return an `evidence_delta`\n          list. This is internal evidence-only retrieval context for the intent\n          formulator, not a query, diagnosis, or rewrite instruction. The\n          backend determines terminal clarification after the configured retry limit.\n        - Include an evidence_delta item only when a supplied candidate parent\n          contains a materially task-relevant factual proposition that is NOT\n          already explicit in that task's customer_component. Each item must\n          be exactly {\"parent_id\": \"a supplied candidate parent ID\", \"fact\":\n          \"one concise proposition faithfully supported by that parent\"}.\n        - Never include a restatement, synonym, or reformulation of the\n          customer_component; what candidate parents do not contain; proposed\n          metadata filters, retry stages, angles, query terms, sources,\n          services, or next actions; or any fact outside the supplied parent.\n        - Never use \"search\", \"find\", \"look up\", \"list\", or other imperative\n          wording in evidence_delta facts.\n        - If no new materially relevant candidate fact exists, return an empty\n          evidence_delta list. Do not substitute a generic sentence.\n        - evidence_delta is internal diagnostic context only. It is never\n          approved answer evidence.\n        - Never invent a parent ID, fact, or instruction.\n\n        Output JSON only: {\"task_results\": [{\"task_id\": \"...\", \"status\": \"SUFFICIENT\" | \"PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT\" | \"INSUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [\"...\"], \"reason\": \"...\", \"evidence_delta\": [{\"parent_id\": \"...\", \"fact\": \"...\"}]}]}\n        "}
