rchant coupons, referral bonuses. \n5. Technical & General Support\nAuthentication And Security: Login issues, password/PIN resets, OTP failures, tokens, fraud. \nBranch And ATM Locator: Finding physical infrastructure. \nGeneral Inquiries: Catch-all. App navigation, UI bugs, compliance, generic notifications.\n\n\n    Active Context Matrix: []\n    Current Graph Context: active_plan=False, retrieved_knowledge=False\n    Recalled Prior-Session Context Is Available: False\n    Recent Conversation: Last Session Recall (advisory only; not current state):\nNone\n\nCurrent-Session Rolling Context (advisory only):\nNone\n\nCurrent Session Trusted History (latest 10 turns):\nAI: Welcome back, Benson! How can I help with your banking today?\n\nYou can fulfil your request using the form below.\n\nWould you like to know more about the fee you asked about earlier, or would you still like to complete your Change Address request?\nUser: what is the annual fee for my business credit card. what's process to apply a loan?\n    User Baseline (advisory only; do not treat it as a current request): None\n    Latest User Input (context only; the components above are authoritative): \"what is the annual fee for my business credit card. what's process to apply a loan?\"\n    TASK: Act as a Decoupled Database Search Architect.\n\n    CRITICAL RULES FOR ANGLE QUERIES:\n    - NEVER use conversational filler (e.g., \"Provide a guide\", \"Explain how to\", \"What is\").\n    - NEVER paraphrase the customer's original question in an angle.\n    - Each angle must be a short natural-language PHRASE (8-20 words) that reads like a sentence fragment from an FAQ answer.\n    - Use common banking vocabulary only. Do not invent specific product names, amounts, dates, or branch details.\n\n    1. CONTEXTUAL INHERITANCE: Read each component's customer_component text first. A Product or Intent may be inherited only when it is unambiguously established by the current-session trusted history, Active Context