request and explain internally whether Product, Intent, or both are missing or ambiguous. Do not guess a product or create a generic task merely to fill the array. Also set clarification.customer_facing_question: one short, natural, standalone question a customer would actually be shown, asking only about unresolved_request. It must not assert a product, policy, or fact, and must not attempt to answer any part of the request -- it is rendered as its own separate response element, never combined with anything else, so it must read completely on its own.\n       Also set clarification.candidate_replies: 0-3 plausible guesses at what the customer means, most likely first -- about the Product, the Intent, or whatever specifically is ambiguous here, not necessarily a product. Populate this only when genuinely inferable (e.g. an unresolved term with only one plausible matrix match given the customer's wording); leave it empty when you have no real basis to guess (e.g. a term identifying no plausible product or intent at all). Each entry needs a short \"label\" (e.g. \"Personal Loan\") and a \"message\" that is a complete, natural sentence a customer would actually send (e.g. \"I'm asking about a personal loan.\") -- never a bare word or phrase as the message.\n    7. SCOPE DECLINE: For a DECLINE component, set decline.reason to a short, factual statement and decline.category per Rule 3's two cases. For category=\"out_of_scope_product\", only decline when the matrix confirms no matching BASE product family exists at all — never guess, and never decline merely because a qualified or branded variant of an existing base product is unfamiliar. For category=\"individual_customers_only\", name the non-individual segment (e.g., business, corporate) in decline.reason without asserting whether Horizon does or does not serve that segment in reality — only that this assistant's information does not cover it. Also set decline.customer_facing_message: one short, natural, standalone sentence a customer would actually be shown, following the same category rule as decline.reason. It is rendered as its own separate response element, never combined with anything else, so it must read completely on its own.\n    8. Use \"ALL\" only when a component is genuinely universal and its Intent is a valid intent listed under \"ALL\" in the Product/Intent Matrix. \"ALL\" is not a fallback for an unknown product.\n\n    Output JSON ONLY:\n    {\"components\": [{\"component_id\":\"component_1\",\"customer_component\":\"open an account\",\"resolution\":\"SEARCH\",\"search_task\":{\"task_id\":\"task_1\",\"angle_groups\":[{\"group_id\":\"base\",\"procedural\":\"...\",\"policy\":\"...\",\"conceptual\":\"...\"}],\"target_commercial_product\":\"Deposit_Account\",\"target_intent\":[\"Application\"]},\"clarification\":null,\"decline\":null},{\"component_id\":\"component_2\",\"customer_component\":\"the fee\",\"resolution\":\"CLARIFY\",\"search_task\":null,\"clarification\":{\"clarification_id\":\"intent_clarification_1\",\"unresolved_request\":\"the fee\",\"reason\":\"No product or service is identified.\",\"customer_facing_question\":\"Could you let me know which product or service this fee question is about?\",\"candidate_replies\":[]},\"decline\":null},{\"component_id\":\"component_5\",\"customer_component\":\"how to apply for a loan\",\"resolution\":\"CLARIFY\",\"search_task\":null,\"clarification\":{\"clarification_id\":\"intent_clarification_2\",\"unresolved_request\":\"loan\",\"reason\":\"Personal_Loan is the only loan-type matrix product, but the customer's intended type is not confirmed.\",\"customer_facing_question\":\"Could you confirm you're asking about a personal loan?\",\"candidate_replies\":[{\"label\":\"Personal Loan\",\"message\":\"I'm asking about a personal loan.\"}]},\"decline\":null},{\"component_id\":\"component_3\",\"customer_component\":\"margin trading account\",\"resolution\":\"DECLINE\",\"search_task\":null,\"clarification\":null,\"decline\":{\